- [ ] 1.1 Add a pure candidate-diversification helper that derives a signature only from direct `SearchCandidate` fields and explicitly bounded catalog-text markers; return no signature for missing, malformed, or ambiguous evidence, and verify this behavior with focused unit tests.
- [ ] 1.2 Implement deterministic bounded diversification over the RRF-ranked union: keep the first representative of every non-null signature, keep ungroupable candidates eligible, then fill remaining slots in the existing rank order; verify representative selection, tie stability, capacity, and no-duplicate cases with focused unit tests.

## 2. Hybrid retrieval integration

- [ ] 2.1 Apply the helper after existing candidate merge/RRF calculation and before the configured hybrid reranker cutoff, without issuing requests or changing RRF scores; verify with mocked dense/BM25 stores that a distinct lower-ranked variant displaces only a redundant candidate.
- [ ] 2.2 Preserve original-query/alternate-query retrieval, per-modality LD-id de-duplication, and fallback when structural signature extraction errors; verify with focused `HybridRetriever` regression tests.

## 3. Matching regression coverage

- [ ] 3.1 Add or update a mocked matcher integration test confirming the reranker receives the diversified list but the normalized source tender string remains the reranker query and `MatchResult.query`.
